# Persist LIVE parameter values back into the YAML files on disk.
#
# The problem it solves: `ros2 param set` (and the dashboard's tuning sliders,
# which are the same call) change a running node and nothing else. Reboot the
# robot and a tuning session evaporates. This service snapshots what the node
# is ACTUALLY running right now and writes those numbers into the config file.
#
# It reads from the LIVE NODE, not from whatever the dashboard thinks it sent.
# If a set_parameters call was rejected, or a node clamped a value, the file
# gets the value the robot is really using — the running robot is the source of
# truth, never the UI.

# Node names to snapshot, WITHOUT a leading slash: ['balance_controller'].
# Empty means every node the backend has a config file mapping for.
string[] nodes

# Dry run: work out the diff and report it, write nothing. Use it to see what
# a Save would do before committing to it.
bool preview
---
bool success
string message

# One line per value written, as 'node.param: old -> new'. On a preview this is
# what WOULD be written. Empty means nothing had drifted from the file.
string[] changed
